[{:db/id 17592186119830 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-685229d2-34f8-5173-a67b-785ec23ea6ca"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-685229d2-34f8-5173-a67b-785ec23ea6ca" :question/id #uuid "685229d2-34f8-5173-a67b-785ec23ea6ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-127876" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨2,-1,3⟩=17.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨2,-1,3⟩=17$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨2,-1,3⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-1,3⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+3{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,2{t}_{1}+3{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,2,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-df160bc6-de12-5b0e-ab4a-f86e448d27ab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-df160bc6-de12-5b0e-ab4a-f86e448d27ab" :answer-field/id #uuid "df160bc6-de12-5b0e-ab4a-f86e448d27ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c7324eda-c77e-5439-bf52-4a39226f0238" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e17bf533-f3b3-5889-bc5d-63042f883173" "answer-c9e7ce1b-ea58-5c77-a5f2-354c10202f64" "answer-c7324eda-c77e-5439-bf52-4a39226f0238" "answer-b1bdd0cd-8af9-54f9-913d-1f9c797b10c9" "answer-37d331a3-d216-56b1-b1e8-c1c659788885"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e17bf533-f3b3-5889-bc5d-63042f883173" :answer/id #uuid "e17bf533-f3b3-5889-bc5d-63042f883173" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9e7ce1b-ea58-5c77-a5f2-354c10202f64" :answer/id #uuid "c9e7ce1b-ea58-5c77-a5f2-354c10202f64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7324eda-c77e-5439-bf52-4a39226f0238" :answer/id #uuid "c7324eda-c77e-5439-bf52-4a39226f0238" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1bdd0cd-8af9-54f9-913d-1f9c797b10c9" :answer/id #uuid "b1bdd0cd-8af9-54f9-913d-1f9c797b10c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37d331a3-d216-56b1-b1e8-c1c659788885" :answer/id #uuid "37d331a3-d216-56b1-b1e8-c1c659788885" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152193 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ad9f5224-cb10-5d73-824c-c4a1c6b129db"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ad9f5224-cb10-5d73-824c-c4a1c6b129db" :question/id #uuid "ad9f5224-cb10-5d73-824c-c4a1c6b129db" :question/math-academy-id "q-79834" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)=x{e}^{-3x}$ is a solution to the equation ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+9y=0,$ then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n\nI. $y(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{-3x}$\n\nII. $y(x)=x{e}^{1-3x}$\n\nIII. $y(x)=\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}$" :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, if the function ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, and $c$ is a constant, then $y(x)=c{y}_{1}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{-3x}=x\\cdot x{e}^{-3x}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of a non-constant function and a known solution.\n\n- The function $y(x)=x{e}^{1-3x}=e\\cdot x{e}^{-3x}$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. In this case, $c=e.$\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. In this case, $c=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8da06cc9-b0c5-52b6-84dd-18ec2eed5c30"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8da06cc9-b0c5-52b6-84dd-18ec2eed5c30" :answer-field/id #uuid "8da06cc9-b0c5-52b6-84dd-18ec2eed5c30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1852cf18-7940-5ffb-b6e9-07dc2d8b3ffb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0448241b-1ccb-508e-86a5-d20799033a9d" "answer-ffe77668-6986-532b-ad24-452a980f2a61" "answer-4b70160a-7cf4-5dc0-b625-a1f5e3aaac47" "answer-1852cf18-7940-5ffb-b6e9-07dc2d8b3ffb" "answer-372838a6-d8fb-5b8c-828c-49e4aef7bf85"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0448241b-1ccb-508e-86a5-d20799033a9d" :answer/id #uuid "0448241b-1ccb-508e-86a5-d20799033a9d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ffe77668-6986-532b-ad24-452a980f2a61" :answer/id #uuid "ffe77668-6986-532b-ad24-452a980f2a61" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b70160a-7cf4-5dc0-b625-a1f5e3aaac47" :answer/id #uuid "4b70160a-7cf4-5dc0-b625-a1f5e3aaac47" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1852cf18-7940-5ffb-b6e9-07dc2d8b3ffb" :answer/id #uuid "1852cf18-7940-5ffb-b6e9-07dc2d8b3ffb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-372838a6-d8fb-5b8c-828c-49e4aef7bf85" :answer/id #uuid "372838a6-d8fb-5b8c-828c-49e4aef7bf85" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124628 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-110b21f6-4be1-556e-b1d2-7f471afa85fc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-110b21f6-4be1-556e-b1d2-7f471afa85fc" :question/id #uuid "110b21f6-4be1-556e-b1d2-7f471afa85fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-94645" :question/problem "Let $R$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\nI. ${I}_{2}\\in R$\n\nII. For every $A,B\\in R,$ we have $A+B\\in R.$\n\nIII. The set is closed under addition." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $R$ contains only matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers. However, ${I}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ is *not* a matrix of this form. So, ${I}_{2}\\notin R.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, suppose $A=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\in R$ and $B=[\\begin{aligned}c & d \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\in R,$ where $a,b,c,d$ are real numbers. Then, \n\n$$\nA+B=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c & d \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a+c & b+d \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $(a+c)$ and $(b+d)$ are real numbers, we conclude that $[\\begin{aligned}a+c & b+d \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\in R,$ i.e. $A+B\\in R.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set is closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5e68d1f8-4799-5165-aca8-846dbe8edad9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5e68d1f8-4799-5165-aca8-846dbe8edad9" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e68d1f8-4799-5165-aca8-846dbe8edad9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d02e0e83-d95c-5ac9-a67d-e710736e75a3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5b92cdf9-7bbc-5a4d-bde4-9015e4683e5e" "answer-b4dee0f7-a23a-5d52-9410-5af27ff4ea58" "answer-d02e0e83-d95c-5ac9-a67d-e710736e75a3" "answer-7099a231-0e75-582a-b5c5-f1a18019b145" "answer-3e57d8cf-406d-5f34-b194-cd33686b0e87"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b92cdf9-7bbc-5a4d-bde4-9015e4683e5e" :answer/id #uuid "5b92cdf9-7bbc-5a4d-bde4-9015e4683e5e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4dee0f7-a23a-5d52-9410-5af27ff4ea58" :answer/id #uuid "b4dee0f7-a23a-5d52-9410-5af27ff4ea58" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d02e0e83-d95c-5ac9-a67d-e710736e75a3" :answer/id #uuid "d02e0e83-d95c-5ac9-a67d-e710736e75a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7099a231-0e75-582a-b5c5-f1a18019b145" :answer/id #uuid "7099a231-0e75-582a-b5c5-f1a18019b145" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e57d8cf-406d-5f34-b194-cd33686b0e87" :answer/id #uuid "3e57d8cf-406d-5f34-b194-cd33686b0e87" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186354557 :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{{x}^{3}},\\, & 3<x<6, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115850 :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${A}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-66d030fe-89ea-590e-a4c4-c2634bad9dc1" :activity/id #uuid "66d030fe-89ea-590e-a4c4-c2634bad9dc1" :activity/title "Quiz 10" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-03ba6058-aa73-5c10-8748-85baeda7b617" "step-592ffa31-ea8f-51b8-937f-906bbedb24cc" "step-d1b56378-cb65-59f2-83b1-0d3e81ad2784" "step-02bcbecd-c304-5e2b-8f28-c57c6264ce6f" "step-6c624bbe-499a-5790-8fed-185eae3fd6f7" "step-a7953375-8260-5b48-96cf-294e5e98fca1" "step-9a6659c3-30bd-5fc8-b681-0409680334f9" "step-5b5f4e70-6185-51b2-b8c3-b5694bc863ef"] :activity/first-step "step-03ba6058-aa73-5c10-8748-85baeda7b617" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-03ba6058-aa73-5c10-8748-85baeda7b617" :step/id #uuid "03ba6058-aa73-5c10-8748-85baeda7b617" :step/content 17592186377695 :step/next "step-592ffa31-ea8f-51b8-937f-906bbedb24cc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-592ffa31-ea8f-51b8-937f-906bbedb24cc" :step/id #uuid "592ffa31-ea8f-51b8-937f-906bbedb24cc" :step/content "question-685229d2-34f8-5173-a67b-785ec23ea6ca" :step/next "step-d1b56378-cb65-59f2-83b1-0d3e81ad2784" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d1b56378-cb65-59f2-83b1-0d3e81ad2784" :step/id #uuid "d1b56378-cb65-59f2-83b1-0d3e81ad2784" :step/content 17592186290277 :step/next "step-02bcbecd-c304-5e2b-8f28-c57c6264ce6f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-02bcbecd-c304-5e2b-8f28-c57c6264ce6f" :step/id #uuid "02bcbecd-c304-5e2b-8f28-c57c6264ce6f" :step/content "question-ad9f5224-cb10-5d73-824c-c4a1c6b129db" :step/next